# OpsPilot workspace
#
# Runtime environment files live next to each app, not at the repo root.
# Bun, Nest, and Next.js load `.env*` from the app working directory.
#
# Setup (current): hosted Supabase for PostgreSQL — no local Docker required.
#   cp apps/api/.env.example apps/api/.env
#   cp apps/web/.env.example apps/web/.env.local
# Then put Supabase Database + API values in apps/api/.env only.
#
# Do not put secrets in this file or in any committed example.

# Optional. Local tooling defaults to development when unset.
# NODE_ENV=development

# Local Docker Compose (compose.yaml) is optional and unused while developing
# against Supabase. If you enable it later, override container settings with a
# gitignored root `.env` if needed:
#   POSTGRES_DB=opspilot
#   POSTGRES_USER=opspilot
#   POSTGRES_PASSWORD=opspilot
#   POSTGRES_PORT=5432
# API connection settings always belong in apps/api/.env
# (DATABASE_URL and/or DATABASE_HOST, DATABASE_PORT, DATABASE_NAME,
# DATABASE_USER, DATABASE_PASSWORD, DATABASE_SSL), not here.
